THIRD-PARTY AND DERIVED SOURCES
===============================

The Fortran sources under source/ include code adapted from earlier programs.
Their origin and status are recorded here. This file is a statement of what is
currently known; it will be updated as provenance is confirmed.

1. source/spheres/defmtr.f90, empty.f90, radii.f90, utils.f90

   Fortran 90 adaptations of the sphere routines (EMPTYSPHERES, EMPTY, GETEPOS,
   REGET_RE, DEFMTR, RADII, ...) of the SPR-KKR/xband package (H. Ebert and
   co-workers; the sources carry SPAG headers dated 26 March 2020). Those
   routines in turn build on the LMTO47 program (the Stuttgart LMTO lineage of
   O. K. Andersen, O. Jepsen and co-workers).

   STATUS: written permission from the copyright holders to redistribute these
   files under the GNU GPL v3 has NOT yet been confirmed. They must not be
   published or distributed under this licence until it has been.

2. source/spheres/utils.f90 (additionally)

   Contains auxiliary routines originating from the netlib reference
   LAPACK (version 2.0) and BLAS libraries (DLAMC1-DLAMC5, LSAME, IDAMAX,
   DCOPY, DSCAL and related helpers), and an atomic Dirac-equation solver
   (RHFDS and its helpers) of the same xband/LMTO47 lineage as item 1.

3. source/potpars/lmto_lib.f90, source/potpars/potpar_wrapper.f90,
   source/io/atom_io.f90

   Default potential-parameter tables and formulas (DEFPP, DEFMOM, DEFCNF,
   screening constants) follow the LMTO47 conventions; source comments cite
   "Kampur notes" (Eq. 3.94) and the screening constants of O. Jepsen.
   STATUS: a routine-by-routine provenance audit has not been completed.

An independent comparison with the Questaal package found no evidence that
these routines were copied from Questaal (whose empty-sphere finder, FINDES,
is a separate implementation); Questaal's licence therefore does not apply to
them.
